Upstream re-derives the last-used session from disk config any time
`entering_name || username != selected_username` is true -- which also
fires just from re-confirming the already-selected username (e.g.
tabbing back into the username field). That clobbers a session the user
just picked from the dropdown with their old saved default. Only fall
back to the last-used session when the username actually changed.

